course: dictionary
lesson: 685
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Balsam is a good example. It can be a sticky, sweet-smelling oil, a soothing cream, a tree, or a garden plant.
explain: «Gorse, broom and Himalayan balsam have pods that dry and twist on hot dry days until they burst and fling the seeds out.» Here balsam is a plant, not a cream. The clues are pods, seeds and bursting.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about a lip balm or a cough, balsam means a soothing cream. If it is about trees or resin, it means the sticky oil or the tree that gives it. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Balsam means a sweet-smelling, sticky oil or resin from certain trees.
fact: Balsam can also mean a soothing cream or ointment, like a balm.
fact: A balsam fir is a tree that gives this resin.
fact: Balsam is also a garden plant with bright flowers, also called impatiens or busy Lizzie.
fact: «Himalayan balsam» is a weed by rivers in the UK, and its seed pods burst open when touched.
exercise: «Gorse, broom and Himalayan balsam have pods that dry and twist on hot dry days.» In this sentence, what is Himalayan balsam? | A cough sweet | A soothing cream for dry skin | A tall, healthy tree | *A plant with pods that burst open and fling out seeds
exercise: A label on a lip balm lists balsam. What does balsam mean here? | A garden plant with bright flowers | A tree bark used for building | *A soothing cream or ointment | A loud, sharp noise
exercise: Find and copy the word from the sentence that means to throw out with force. | hot | *fling | pods | dry
test: What kind of tree is a balsam fir? | *A tree that gives a sweet-smelling resin | A tree with bright red berries | An oak tree with acorns | A palm tree from a hot island
test: In a story, a room smelled of balsam, calm and healing. What does balsam suggest? | A loud crash | A smell of burning toast | *A calm, healing, sweet smell | A harsh, bitter smell
exam: Which meaning of balsam fits a lip balm label? | A sharp, bitter drink | A tree bark used for building | A garden plant with exploding pods | *A soothing cream or ointment
